    "synopsis": {
        "native": "Le concours d\u2019entr\u00e9e de la F\u00e9mis, Grande Ecole de cin\u00e9ma, film\u00e9 pour la premi\u00e8re fois. A travers ce documentaire, Claire Simon questionne le rapport entre les g\u00e9n\u00e9rations et le difficile parcours de s\u00e9lection qu'organisent nos soci\u00e9t\u00e9s contemporaines.",
        "english": "With Place aux jeunes, Claire Simon will delve into the daily life of the Parisian cinema school, la F\u00e9mis, where a specific Republican ideal of excellence is practiced and entry into which can be summed up as follows: \"everyone\u2019s equal, but only the best get in\u2026\". Through the admission process, the hard work all year and the graduation exams, Place aux jeunes will establish a portrait of our relationship to excellence in the Art world and of one of the most prestigious art school in France. A place of culture where generations intermingle."
